Z||000000||Banzai||11-17-2001||12:12 PM||||I just picked up an 86 decklid and wing from a guy I work with($180 pristine condition) and he has a Fiero 2.8 in the garage he  has no use for. He claims the engine has only around 2000 original miles on it. The engine is COMPLETE intake to oil pan with the exhaust manifolds, Y-pipe, and alternator. The engine has the engraved upper plenum and Holley throttle body. The oil filter is black.(is this original?) The heat sheathing on the Y-pipe is in perfect condition as well as the EGR Tube. The intake is in perfect condition but the paint on the valve covers is peeling off from near the exhaust manifolds-up(the engine has been sitting for years, but turns over fine). It also has the engine mount and bracket. MY QUESTIONS-------<P>1. What year is this motor?<BR>2. Should I believe his claims on the mileage?<P>I offered him $200 for the motor and he said he'll take it to get it out of his garage. Seems like the deal of the century.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!<P>"I promise Honey, It'll be done in one MORE week-------"||||reg||10
Z||000001||avengador1||11-17-2001||02:26 PM||||It sounds like an 87(engraved manifold,earler ones had stickers). If the y pipe has insulation wrap on it its an 88.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Banzai||11-18-2001||05:37 AM||||Yes the Y-pipe has the insulation on it. <P>If it is an 88', do I need a computer and harness from an 88' or will any year work. I will be putting it in an 84'. The oil sending unit is on a tube near the front of the motor. Are all V6s like this? There's no cover on the EGR either. Will I be able to adapt the 84' air conditioning to the 88' V6?  The lower bracket is on the motor but I will need the upper. Will my 84' compressor and lines work??<P>I'm sure that this is covered in the archives somewhere but anyones input would be appreciated. Thanks.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!<P>"I promise Honey, it'll be done in one MORE week-------"||||reg||1
